  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.48,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.85,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings sit on a flat plateau at about 1.34 from 7 h to 18 h. A reader that is saturating would produce this plateau. I diluted the retained 18 h aliquot and scaled each reading by its dilution factor. The 10x dilution read 0.1467, which scales to 1.467. The 20x dilution read 0.0737, which scales to 1.474. The 40x dilution read 0.038, which scales to 1.52 but is noisier at that low signal. The replicates at 10x and 20x agree closely. The three dilutions give a consistent corrected OD of about 1.47–1.5. The undiluted reading was 1.34 (1.31–1.37 over 13–18 h), so it falls about 10% short of that level. This is consistent with the undiluted reading being compressed at high OD, so the true late biomass is higher than the undiluted reading indicates. The effect is modest, and I did not run a dilution series on earlier time points, so some uncertainty remains."
  },
